{
	title: 'Account choice is a local.ts hook',
	spec: "The choice of account per request is one replaceable function on the auth object (pickAccount), which local.ts can override, e.g. to prefer one OpenAI account until it runs out. The default prefers subscriptions, always: it ranks the subscription (OAuth) accounts least-used first by their usage windows, not by file order, keeping a session on its chosen subscription for the prompt cache; API keys (the file's in order, then ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY) come after every subscription, since a key has no usage windows and ranked with them would always look least used (that bug spent the user's paid credits while four ChatGPT subscriptions sat idle). A session is on a key only while no subscription is usable (broken or rate limited for the model) and leaves it on the next request once one is. Moving onto a key writes a transcript line naming the key's account name (never its value) and why each subscription was passed over. A key the provider says is out of credits (HTTP 402, OpenAI insufficient_quota or billing codes, which come with a 429, or Anthropic's 'credit balance is too low') is set aside like a broken login until its entry changes, and the request retries at once on the next account; it is never treated as a rate limit and retried on the same key. Model-specific windows such as Anthropic's 7d_sonnet don't affect the choice (all Claude models share one quota) and /status doesn't show them (questions.md 128, 129).",
	status: 'done',
	needs: [],
	foldInto: ['61'],
	notes: [
		'auth.pickAccount is the single local.ts override for per-request routing; returns ordered accounts and preserves session affinity by default. Usage ranking covers subscriptions only; API keys follow them (questions.md 128 was misread as ranking keys too).  auth.test.ts clears ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and OPENAI_API_KEY itself, so running it outside ./test never picks up a real key; account-specific windows (7d_sonnet and 7d-sonnet) are ignored by ranking, terminal/web plan, and /status, while raw observations remain cached.'
	]
}
